{"title":"2012 IMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be a triangle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/d/71db3a6e932b60918a8ec1bfd396edc5dc3cfaf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BCA=90^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the foot of the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be a point in the interior of the segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> be the point on the segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/8/2d857b2c804701b561a5c8c90c400f360d27232c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX$\" width=\"29\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/7/967c418abbd2a5dfacf67a35ab6794fb4f1288ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BK=BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"87\" height=\"14\" />. Similarly, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the point on the segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7a4b9c32938e96f30b59dcb29f410cd4c2e3982.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BX$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/9/cd91195c40fff8e465a6846e99a968ee5f9a8de3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AL=AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"80\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/8/048e20e1ec53027257bf9bbec6a82b0b24f647a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M=\\overline{AL}\\cap \\overline{BK}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"123\" height=\"18\" />. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/d/13ddf9c91a32edc1ab183a2520a46923da7126b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MK=ML$\" width=\"92\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/3/913e49ea63c6c130bb8d9d1c3556b052ecc404f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/2/3326232040d196ce9195f25f47ecbf89da4923db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/a/25a2c33b0b5b23d009a87886fc354934ffc02a18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma&#39;&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"16\" /> be the circumcircle of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, the circle with its center as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and radius as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, and the circle with its center as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and radius as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, Respectively.\nSince the center of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/3/913e49ea63c6c130bb8d9d1c3556b052ecc404f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" /> lies on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, the three circles above are coaxial to line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nLet Line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/8/2d857b2c804701b561a5c8c90c400f360d27232c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX$\" width=\"29\" height=\"13\" /> and Line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7a4b9c32938e96f30b59dcb29f410cd4c2e3982.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BX$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> collide with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/3/913e49ea63c6c130bb8d9d1c3556b052ecc404f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/6/56612437b6d768ff5aeea9f567e3671a96a7352a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\neq A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" />) and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/0/8502a4b2fdd2960b1a9df53dc78dd2c9fe69efc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\neq B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" />), Respectively. Also let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/5/0a51e79d352293f49ecb0f60cc043be3050665fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R = AQ \\cap BP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"117\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nThen, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/f/33f7e43d42a92074b57eecaf23e9ecc000c497b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AYB = \\angle AZB = 90^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"187\" height=\"15\" />, by ceva's theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Since triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/e/6ce2cd123db24a7b8373999aea7a98927e3b3c81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> are similar, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/5/f1579e26fe7bea2d9021dde1c708353e8452e29b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AL^2 = AC^2 = AD \\cdot AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"190\" height=\"17\" />, Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/4/7f413dd4c4da1e6db5f2c54aec064a699a95cb6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ALD = \\angle ABL$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"134\" height=\"14\" />.\nIn the same way, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/f/1bf0aa9754ecd4169430730341070d06cac3007f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BKD = \\angle BAK$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"144\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/8/ba89dc64d2642f2f572c667bd46f4a45ad82cab4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ARD = \\angle ABQ = \\angle ALD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"216\" height=\"18\" /> making <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/0/4408215dcbfcf718055501da310170ef9eb33ee5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(A, R, L, D)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"96\" height=\"20\" /> concyclic.\nIn the same way, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/0/1e0f1a3f735bd3b3c89ef3407847fc5b36a31eb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(B, R, K, D)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"100\" height=\"20\" /> is concyclic.\n</p><p><br />\nSo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/3/2f309c685d6e7b641190760c49bb320a5f4322d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ADR = \\angle ALR = 90^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"185\" height=\"15\" />, and in the same way <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/f/f6f27063cc666c699a4373d745359a5771fcd0ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BKR = 90^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"110\" height=\"15\" />. Therefore, the lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/a/5aa01b5d848684547c1c941a858542a58d950113.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RK$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/8/cf801af61a8afe871886f6a1a076976764bffc9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RL$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"14\" /> are tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/2/3326232040d196ce9195f25f47ecbf89da4923db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/a/25a2c33b0b5b23d009a87886fc354934ffc02a18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma&#39;&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"16\" />, respectively.\n</p><p><br />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> is the concentric line of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/2/3326232040d196ce9195f25f47ecbf89da4923db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/a/25a2c33b0b5b23d009a87886fc354934ffc02a18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma&#39;&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/d/0cdc3bbbc09c3edb2ec7968496957297040857ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RK^2 = RL^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"98\" height=\"17\" />, Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/3/b83cada5e526a31f230ddf4a7bc7fc33e72479b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RK = RL$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/e/91e297cb8af3d79a5439edaa5f774d51d6f1f3bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RM$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> is in the middle and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/a/07a90b0aef4727d63c8d82b538a47e7c5834e104.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ADR = \\angle BKR = 90^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"190\" height=\"15\" />,\nwe can say triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/6/0562ac022c992b9ddded82b2c0afe2cb4dec649d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RKM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/9/4694717e84da870d8348ffb198cef04e0311ed6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RLM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" /> are congruent. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/8/61817bd39af3a8d3722a00bf98171c8255460bcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KM = LM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"94\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_IMO\" title=\"2012 IMO\">2012 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2012 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2012 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2012 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2012 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2012 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2012 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2012 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2012 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017035107\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.028 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.040 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 345/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 10930/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.894      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.894      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:11982:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017035107 and revision id 289906. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}